=back

Returns boolean: true on success or false on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.4.0.

=head2 SDL_GetDefaultTextureScaleMode

  my $result = SDL_GetDefaultTextureScaleMode($renderer, $scale_mode);

C: C<< _Bool SDL_GetDefaultTextureScaleMode(SDL_Renderer * renderer, SDL_ScaleMode * scale_mode) >>

Get default texture scale mode of the given renderer.

This function should only be called on the main thread.

=over

=item renderer - SDL3::Renderer object or undef. the renderer to get data from.

=item scale_mode - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. a SDL_ScaleMode filled with current default scale mode. See SDL_SetDefaultTextureScaleMode() for the meaning of the value.

